0 0 0 rg
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 50.0 758.0 Td (Sequence-Level Knowledge Distillation \(Kim & Rush, EMNLP 2016\) trains the student model to reproduce the) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 50.0 746.5 Td (teacher's argmax output sequences rather than its internal probability distributions. The student minimises) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 50.0 735.0 Td (standard cross-entropy loss against the teacher's discrete token outputs, treating them as ground-truth) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 50.0 723.5 Td (supervision signals:) Tj ET
0.95 0.97 1.00 rg 50.0 689.5 495.0 20.0 re f
0.05 0.50 0.55 RG 2.50 w 50.0 689.5 m 50.0 709.5 l S
BT /FC 8.5 Tf 60.0 695.5 Td (L_KD\(theta\) = - SUM_{t=1}^{T} log P_student\(y_t^teacher | y_{<t}^teacher, x ; theta\)) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 50.0 683.5 Td (Each training example is formatted using the prompt template that mirrors the inference-time format,) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 50.0 672.0 Td (ensuring the student learns the conditional mapping directly:) Tj ET
0.95 0.97 1.00 rg 0.09 0.18 0.40 RG 0.60 w 50.0 626.0 495.0 28.0 re B
0.09 0.18 0.40 RG 2.50 w 50.0 626.0 m 50.0 654.0 l S
