BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 574.0 Td (JSON Validity \(96% vs 0% baseline\): Post-distillation, the student reliably generates syntactically) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 562.5 Td (valid JSON objects, demonstrating that causal language-model fine-tuning on structured targets) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 551.0 Td (effectively internalises schema constraints. The 4 invalid outputs were cases where the model) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 539.5 Td (generated a valid JSON followed by an extra natural-language sentence.) Tj ET
0.09 0.18 0.40 rg 52.0 529.5 2.5 0 360 arc f
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 526.5 Td (Intent Accuracy \(96%\): The student matches the teacher's intent classification, confirming that) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 515.0 Td (8-class command intent is a learnable pattern well within 70M parameters' capacity. Intent tokens are) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 503.5 Td (high-frequency and appear early in every output sequence, making them easy to reinforce.) Tj ET
0.09 0.18 0.40 rg 52.0 493.5 2.5 0 360 arc f
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 490.5 Td (Date Accuracy \(76%\) - lowest slot: Date expressions are highly context-dependent multi-word spans) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 479.0 Td (\(e.g., 'the week after next', 'the month of may', 'this coming friday'\). The student's greedy decoding) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 467.5 Td (strategy, combined with its small context window capacity, causes it to truncate or misidentify span) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 456.0 Td (boundaries for complex temporal expressions more than the teacher.) Tj ET
0.09 0.18 0.40 rg 52.0 446.0 2.5 0 360 arc f
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 443.0 Td (Time Accuracy \(84%\): Better than date but lower than place. Time expressions containing number-word) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 431.5 Td (hybrids \(e.g., 'seven thirty', 'two hundred'\) occasionally cause boundary confusions, though simple) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 420.0 Td (forms \('six am', 'five pm'\) are reproduced accurately.) Tj ET
0.09 0.18 0.40 rg 52.0 410.0 2.5 0 360 arc f
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 407.0 Td (Place Accuracy \(96%\): City and location names are lexically distinctive, typically capitalised proper) Tj ET
BT /FR 8.5 Tf 60.0 395.5 Td (nouns infrequent in pre-training data, making them easy to copy verbatim from the input command.) Tj ET
